    {
      "time": "06:00",
      "night": false,
      "phase": "full",
      "dark": true,
      "notch": 18,
      "want_source": "fallback-gift",
      "nth": 7,
      "of": 12,
      "presage": "La nuit soudain s’épaissit, non par le temps qui passe, mais par la volonté d’un être sans nom qui tire sur les étoffes du ciel, et la pleine lune pâlit comme si elle avait vieilli d’un seul souffle. Sept ombres s’étirent sur le chemin de pierres, immobiles, et le froid arrive avant que le vent ne souffle. Au seuil, le chien ne lève pas la tête, seulement son regard reste — et la clarté s’en va, comme si la nuit, lasse de jouer, avait tout mangé.",
      "presage_en": "The night thickens all at once, not by the passing of time but by the will of a nameless one drawing tight on the sky’s cloth, and the full moon pales as if it has aged in a single breath. Seven shadows stretch along the stone path, still as death, and the cold comes before the wind even stirs. At the threshold the dog does not lift its head, only its gaze stays — and the light slips away, as if the night, tired of playing, has eaten it all.",
      "score": [
        {
          "note": "D",
          "start": "0",
          "duration": "2",
